  nodeAbstract: "\r"
  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What is an Insulin Dimer?
    basic: Two insulin monomers join to form a dimer and three dimers join to form
      a hexamer.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "Insulin dimers result from elevated insulin concentration in vesicles.
      \nThe dimers are stabilized via an intermolecular beta sheet formed by the
      two beta strands on the B chain. \nCoincidentally, this beta strand is also
      the active binding site for insulin receptors, therefore making insulin dimers
      inactive."
